==Trivia==
*Rampage Cats were among the units that were given [[Immune to Warp]] in [[Version 6.5 Update|Version 6.5]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Sports Day Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Sports Day Cat
The power of three Cats, and one Tank Cat.
These cats love Sports Day and
always strive for the top team (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Kidnapper Cats
The power of three Cats, and one Tank Cat.
Though an effective team, the Tank Cat
is the victim, apparently. (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Rampage Cats
No one wanted to pay the ransom, so they
just made the Tank into a banner of victory.
Morally ambiguous efficiency! (Area Atk)</pre>
*Rampage Cat's design and Japanese Name, Bo-Taoshi Cat, references [[wikipedia:Bo-taoshi|bo-taoshi]], a famous game similar to capture-the-flag in Japanese sports days.
*In the Taiwanese and Korean version of [[The Battle Cats]], the [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]] is wearing a blue headband.
*Both stat-wise and cost-wise, this unit is a literal combination of three [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cats]] and a [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]].

